troski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.0002710429981625101,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.1,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.04715159716590739,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":32.4,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.06248920676536354,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":12.5,"_gate_pool_share":-0.2227721452210606,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.03629297749855742,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":6.9,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.050784198775584155,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":50.8,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03980392594241083,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":55.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.30995301569337563,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03548933936903937,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":40.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.07794,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":52.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Kinetik Holdings Inc., through its subsidiaries, operates as a midstream company in the Texas Delaware Basin. The company operates through two segments, Midstream Logistics and Pipeline Transportation. It offers gathering, compression, processing, stabilization, treating, and storage services; transportation services through pipelines; and water gathering and disposal services for companies that produce natural gas, natural gas liquids (NGL), and crude oil. The company also sells condensates, natural gas residue, and NGLs. Kinetik Holdings Inc. was founded in 2017 and is headquartered in Midland, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jamie W. Welch | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 500 people. Revenue per employee of $3.5M ranks in the above the sector median among Energy peers. Each employee generates $223K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $125K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Kinetik Holdings Inc. is a mid-cap energy business with a $9.3B market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $112M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.39\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 7.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries a 167% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.673214797820476},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $188.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Kinetik Holdings (KNTK) Stock Getting Too Expensive On Earnings?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-kntk/kinetik-holdings/news/is-kinetik-holdings-kntk-stock-getting-too-expensive-on-earn","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794486347.128,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.916,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (KNTK) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/23/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_KNTK_Price_Events_111226063601_1794483361